vine 1.2.0
prefix: sorg
title: Scout organization remediation
---
[sorg] Reduce Scout to its least-entangled necessary features (planning)
Scout carries features that exist only to retire other features, facts declared
in three places, and a tree whose shape is held together by path arithmetic.
This graph plans the remediation ahead of extraction, in the order the
measurements imply: rule what is necessary, delete what is not, then lay out
what remains.
Complete when extracted-Scout's necessary capability surface is the only thing
in the tree, and moving a file costs nothing.
-> sorg/verify/organization
> Necessity precedes layout. The cheapest description of an unnecessary feature is zero, so no relocation of a feature happens before its survival is ruled.
> The unit of feature is the public capability surface: MCP tools and CLI subcommands. Necessity is judged against Scout-as-extracted, not against localmodal's trial.
> Measurements in the attached proposal are dated to 2026-07-24 at e751fec and are re-runnable; a claim that has drifted is remeasured rather than argued.
@guidance text/markdown proposals/scout-organization.md
@guidance text/markdown proposals/scout-vocabulary.md
---
[sorg/design/necessary-capabilities] Design with user: the surviving capability surface (planning)
Rule which public capabilities extracted Scout has: the source tools
(scout_search, source_read, source_propose, refresh_stale), the CLI
subcommands, web_search, and the retired set (legacy aliases, vendor fetch
scripts, migrate). Measured footprints: web_search 661 lines across 4 modules
touching the engine at zero points; legacy aliases 640; vendor fetchers 281;
migrate 208.
web_search is separable at zero cost either way, which makes it the one
capability whose ruling can be deferred cheaply.
Accept: the owner names the surviving list and the retired list, and every
module in the attached reachability table belongs to exactly one of them.
---
[sorg/design/activation-residue] Design with user: what remains of activation (planning)
activation.py is 96 lines, fan-in 6, and the only module reachable from all six
capabilities; its job is sequencing the legacy cutover so a legacy reader
cannot fall back. With the retired capabilities gone there is no reader to
fence out, but "has this store ever published?" may remain a necessary state
distinct from "has the cutover happened?".
Owns the fate of the ACTIVATED marker, transition_lock, is_source_control_active,
and the BOOTSTRAP_AFTER_ACTIVATION and LEGACY_MIGRATION_REQUIRED diagnostic
codes.
Accept: the owner rules which states survive, where they live, and which
diagnostic codes leave the closed union.
-> sorg/design/necessary-capabilities
---
[sorg/design/root-provenance] Design with user: where a root comes from (planning)
29 of 53 modules derive their own location from __file__; 9 take a root
parameter; 15 need neither. Rule how a root reaches the code that needs one,
and name the exact set of entrypoints permitted to derive it.
This node owns location provenance for every caller including tests; it does
not own what a test is allowed to address.
Accept: the owner selects one provenance and names the permitted deriving set,
such that a module's physical position stops being load-bearing.
---
[sorg/design/test-coupling] Design with user: what a test may address (planning)
The split preserved the pre-split module object as a patch address:
source_control/__init__ re-exports the surface and owns runtime seams, and
plane.py and execution.py resolve the package through sys.modules[__package__]
at call time. harness.py loads engine modules by file path with a fallback
branch that detects whether a name has become a package.
Rule what a test is permitted to reach: the public surface, named seams, or
module internals.
Accept: the owner rules the addressable surface, and the runtime self-reference
either has a stated reason to remain or a replacement.
---
[sorg/design/process-topology] Design with user: one program or two (planning)
scout/server holds exactly one import edge into the engine and reaches
everything else by spawning two long-lived workers over line-JSON pipes. At
runtime scout/ and resources/ behave like two programs; in the tree they look
like two folders of one. Retiring the legacy aliases retires one of the two
workers, which changes the question rather than answering it.
Accept: the owner rules whether the surviving worker is a peer process or an
internal detail, since that decides whether the two directories may merge.
-> sorg/design/necessary-capabilities
---
[sorg/measure/capability-tracing] Trace capabilities to methods, not modules (notstarted)
Module-level reachability cannot separate scout_search from source_propose:
both enter through the SourceControl facade, so all 17 core modules appear
shared by every source capability. Trace at method level instead, so read and
mutate are shown to be one factor or two.
Report data: per-capability module and method sets, and the modules that serve
exactly one capability.
Accept: the over-approximation recorded in the proposal is replaced by a
measured split, or is shown to be the true answer.
---
[sorg/measure/fence-cost] Measure the cost of a stratum fence (notstarted)
The import graph is 8 strata with zero static cycles, but directory membership
predicts nothing about what a module may import. Measure which current edges
would become illegal if directories encoded strata.
Report data: the illegal-edge list, or its absence.
Accept: the evidence shows whether tree-as-permission costs anything today or
is free because the graph is already clean.
---
[sorg/remove/legacy-readers] Retire the pre-activation reader path (notstarted)
Owns resources/search.py (640 lines, including the second CURRENT pointer the
design ruled must never be read as truth), resources/freshness.py (114), the
tracked resources/sources.json freshness ledger, and the legacy alias routing
and unconditional startup spawn in scout/server.py, which today pays an index
and model load on every server start for a route that post-activation
delegates elsewhere.
Accept: no alias resolves through a pre-activation index, and no second index
pointer exists in the tree.
-> sorg/design/activation-residue
---
[sorg/remove/vendor-fetchers] Retire the per-vendor fetch scripts (notstarted)
Owns resources/fetch_modal_docs.py, resources/fetch_papers.py, and
resources/fetch_vscode_docs.py (281 lines), whose onboarding role was replaced
by the public propose and refresh-stale commands.
Accept: no onboarding path requires a bespoke vendor script, and the checked-in
material they produced is reachable only as declared sources.
-> sorg/design/activation-residue
---
[sorg/remove/legacy-migration] Retire the one-shot legacy import (notstarted)
Owns resources/source_migration.py (208 lines), resources/initial-sources.json,
and the migrate and write-migration-manifest CLI subcommands. The private
bootstrap path on the control plane is a separate surface and is not in scope
here.
Accept: the migration entrypoints are gone and no surviving command depends on
the legacy manifest.
-> sorg/design/activation-residue
---
[sorg/remove/transition-tests] Retire the transition-only test coverage (notstarted)
Owns scout/tests/test_corpus.py, test_freshness.py,
test_legacy_activation_guard.py, test_activation_marker.py (174 lines
together), and the legacy leg of test_machine_output.py.
Accept: the suite covers only surviving behavior, and no removed test was
carrying an assertion about a surviving feature.
-> sorg/remove/legacy-migration
-> sorg/remove/legacy-readers
-> sorg/remove/vendor-fetchers
---
[sorg/implement/activation-residue] Apply the activation ruling (notstarted)
Implement whatever the ruling leaves: the surviving state, its home, and the
closed diagnostic union with the retired codes removed. Lands only once the
capabilities that consumed the marker are gone.
Accept: the union is closed over surviving codes, and no surviving module
imports a concept whose only job was the cutover.
-> sorg/design/activation-residue
-> sorg/remove/transition-tests
---
[sorg/implement/dispatch-surface] Describe the command surface once (notstarted)
source_cli.main and source_worker._reply are two dispatch tables over the same
five control-plane operations, 76 and 68 lines, each with separately written
argument validation and error rendering. The design ruled that both a CLI and
an MCP surface exist; it did not rule that the mapping be written twice.
Accept: adding or changing an operation is a single-site edit, and both
surfaces still return the shared control-plane result shape.
-> sorg/design/necessary-capabilities
-> sorg/remove/legacy-migration
---
[sorg/implement/embedding-identity] Declare the embedding model once (notstarted)
resources/search.py, resources/source_index.py, and resources/vine.py each
declare MODEL = sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 independently, and the
VINE windower derives its token budget from the identity it declares for
itself. Three descriptions of one fact, where a silent divergence would produce
segments that exceed the index's real encoder limit.
Accept: one declaration, and the windower's budget is derived from the same
value the index is built with.
-> sorg/remove/legacy-readers
---
[sorg/implement/root-provenance] Remove derived location from non-entrypoints (notstarted)
Apply the ruled provenance: config.py's CONFIG_PATH, the two mixed derivers,
and the 18 test modules that rebind __file__ to scout/smoke.py so that
parents[1] arithmetic still lands on the repo root. test_ledger.py additionally
computes a subprocess PYTHONPATH from that rebound value.
Accept: no module outside the permitted deriving set references __file__ for
location, and the suite passes without any module asserting a false position.
-> sorg/design/root-provenance
---
[sorg/implement/location-check] Make location-dependence an executable check (notstarted)
The census that produced the 29/9/15 split is ~60 lines and already the shape
of the check. Give it a threshold and a home so a regression fails loudly
rather than being found by the next refactor.
Accept: introducing a derived location outside the permitted set fails the
check.
-> sorg/implement/root-provenance
---
[sorg/implement/patch-seam] Apply the test-coupling ruling (notstarted)
Implement the ruled addressable surface: the sys.modules[__package__]
self-reference in plane.py and execution.py, the re-export and seam ownership
in source_control/__init__.py, and harness.py's file-path module loader with
its package-detection fallback.
Accept: no test addresses a module object that exists only to reproduce a
pre-split namespace.
-> sorg/design/test-coupling
---
[sorg/design/tree] Design with user: the tree that remains (planning)
With necessity ruled, the removals landed, and location no longer load-bearing,
choose the layout: whether resources/ and scout/ merge, whether directories
encode strata, whether a src/ layout applies, where the checked-in
configuration lives, and how corpus material ships once it is a materialized
source rather than package data.
Accept: the owner selects one layout, and every surviving module has exactly
one home under it.
-> sorg/design/process-topology
-> sorg/design/root-provenance
-> sorg/measure/capability-tracing
-> sorg/measure/fence-cost
---
[sorg/implement/tree] Move to the ruled layout under one import discipline (notstarted)
Apply the selected layout as one change, collapsing the four ways a caller
currently reaches engine code: bare-name flat namespace, package-relative
imports, importlib loading by file path, and subprocess spawn by absolute
path.
Accept: one import discipline holds across the tree, the smoke suite is green
before and after, and no spawn target is addressed by a path computed from a
module's own position.
-> sorg/design/tree
-> sorg/implement/patch-seam
-> sorg/implement/root-provenance
-> sorg/remove/transition-tests
---
[sorg/implement/diagnostic-repair-paths] Decouple repair text from the tree (notstarted)
Diagnostic repair strings name invocation paths such as resources/source_cli.py,
so the closed error union carries knowledge of the file layout and goes stale
at extraction.
Accept: a diagnostic's repair instruction survives a layout change without
edits, or its dependence on one is deliberate and stated.
-> sorg/design/tree
---
[sorg/verify/organization] Verify the remediated organization (notstarted)
Re-run the capability, strata, location, and filesystem-ownership measurements
against the remediated tree and record the deltas beside the 2026-07-24
baseline. Exercise every surviving capability through both CLI and MCP.
Report data: measured line and module counts per capability, the location
census, and the surviving diagnostic union.
Accept: every surviving capability behaves identically to its pre-remediation
behavior, and no measurement shows a feature that serves no capability.
-> sorg/implement/activation-residue
-> sorg/implement/diagnostic-repair-paths
-> sorg/implement/dispatch-surface
-> sorg/implement/embedding-identity
-> sorg/implement/location-check
-> sorg/implement/tree
